From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] setup: skip native extension probe when cross-compiling

The pure Python implementation uses ctypes at runtime. Avoid loading the
target C library from the host Python process while preparing the wheel.

Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
---
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -90,7 +90,7 @@
 
 
 ext_mod = []
-if compile_ext_mod or should_compile_ext_mod():
+if compile_ext_mod:
     # add -fpic if x86_64 arch
     if platform in ["linux-x86_64"]:
         os.environ["CFLAGS"] = "-fpic"
